Ladybird now commits an animated custom property from the animation’s
finish event, while its element runs another animation, rather than
crashing. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.78, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5,
the new test commits --x: 0px for each of its three elements in all
three engines, as Ladybird now does. The crash came from a cache of
interval values that Ladybird keeps on its published animation effects,
which has no counterpart to compare in the other engines.
